WEBVTT

00:00:41.939 --> 00:00:49.649
100 yards. She has amnesia. Who knows where she could wander if she blacked out again?

00:00:49.649 --> 00:01:40.500
Well, stay along, Columbus. I'm going to chart my own course to find her. You know me? You know who I am?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.980
You really don't remember, didn't you?

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:53.299
This guy Finley. He locked me in this room saying he's protecting me. Can you get me out of here?

00:01:53.299 --> 00:02:00.299
Does McGever blush every time he walks past me? I'll get something to Jimmy DeLock.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:06.650
This is none of your business.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.650
Kinley, put the gun down, okay?

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.650
Let her go!

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:17.139
Come on, man, look! Is it really worth killing her to get to me?

00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:20.139
Rhetorical question, Lex!

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.139
Vinley, don't do this.

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:24.139
I won't let you get her, Linda!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.290
You okay?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.290
Sure, what's not too great about waking up this morning?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.790
He called me Kara.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.790
Kara Kent. I'm your cousin's friend Lois, whose jeans you've borrowed on more than one occasion.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.329
Lois.

00:04:47.329 --> 00:04:48.329
Lois.

00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:50.329
Look, I know you've got amnesia.

00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:52.329
You must, if you think your type is jail, how chic.

00:04:52.329 --> 00:04:53.329
What's going on?

00:04:53.329 --> 00:04:56.329
Family's just a best boy. That's all.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.329
Great.

00:04:58.329 --> 00:05:00.329
This doesn't exactly look like overtime.

00:05:00.329 --> 00:05:02.329
How did we end up here?

00:05:02.329 --> 00:05:04.329
About...

00:05:04.329 --> 00:05:07.329
A month ago, I lost my memory.

00:05:07.329 --> 00:05:11.329
I wandered off the streets and into a diner where I met a waitress.

00:05:11.329 --> 00:05:15.329
She gave me her couch, got me my job.

00:05:15.329 --> 00:05:17.329
I wanted the diner to me and like family.

00:05:17.329 --> 00:05:19.329
like family.

00:05:19.329 --> 00:05:21.329
Seems like family wants more than a sister.

00:05:21.329 --> 00:05:24.329
He was usually so nice.

00:05:24.329 --> 00:05:27.329
I had no idea he could just snap.

00:05:27.329 --> 00:05:32.779
I can't believe Lex is dead.

00:05:32.779 --> 00:05:38.019
Well, he is.

00:05:38.019 --> 00:05:42.019
And if we don't find a way out of here, we're next.

00:05:42.019 --> 00:05:58.220
Final, how is he?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:01.220
He's in a coma.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:05.220
Thank God we got him Medevac back here from Detroit.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.220
The, um, uh, neurosurface.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.220
Neuro surgeon managed to remove the bullet.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.220
He says that there is a very strong possibility

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:18.220
that Lex may never regain consciousness.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:24.629
I'm sorry.

00:06:24.629 --> 00:06:31.949
We never had a really close relationship.

00:06:31.949 --> 00:06:33.949
A lot was said.

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:38.420
A lot went unsaid.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.420
Clark, I know for a fact that every badge in Michigan

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:47.420
is on this case, and still, no suspects, no witnesses.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.420
I find it hard.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.420
It's hard to believe the shooter would leave Lex in the ditch

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.420
and no one would see anything.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:56.420
Listen, I got a friend in Detroit, a cop.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:00.420
He, uh, called me when he found out about Lex.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.420
He let me borrow this.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:09.259
Kara's alive?

00:07:09.259 --> 00:07:12.259
A picture was taken less than 12 hours ago.

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:14.259
Excuse me. Mr. Luther?

00:07:14.259 --> 00:07:15.259
Yeah.

00:07:15.259 --> 00:07:19.240
Clark, this is Lois' phone.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:22.240
Lois, Kara, and Lex?

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:23.240
Not exactly Three's company.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.240
Cair is wearing a bandage.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.240
a bandage. She may be hurt, which means she doesn't have her powers.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.240
And whoever Lex was dealing with wasn't playing around.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.240
Which means that if Lois and Carer were with him...

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.550
Then they're in danger. We need to find them.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.550
I'll use my healing powers on Lex, and he can tell us where Lois and Kara went.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.550
Chloe, the last time you use your powers, I pulled you out of a morgue refrigerator.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:47.550
Yeah, and then I walked out of there with a clean bill of health and some cold feet.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:50.550
Chloe, if you use your powers again, you could die, permanently.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.550
Or I could just be adjusting to the growing pains. I mean, we don't know.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.550
Nothing happened when I healed Jim.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.550
We have no choice.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:01.550
The only clues we have to where they might be are trapped inside Lex's mind.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:17.139
Couldn't figure out what Lex was doing in Detroit, but I may have found something even more helpful.

00:08:17.139 --> 00:08:19.139
Project Intercept? Is it military?

00:08:19.139 --> 00:08:24.139
Luther Corp developed it for the military to interrogate terrorists by getting inside of their heads.

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:26.139
Literally.

00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:29.139
The entire project was spearheaded by Lionel.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:32.139
Intercept links the suspect in interrogator's brainwaves,

00:08:32.139 --> 00:08:36.139
exposing the interrogator to all the suspect's memories and thoughts.

00:08:36.139 --> 00:08:39.139
You're saying someone could actually go into Lex's mind?

00:08:39.139 --> 00:08:47.700
Where is this thing?

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.700
Luther Corp still owns all the equipment, but it was mothballed six months ago.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:55.700
I can see why. How is this for fine print?

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:02.700
The project worked several times, but then was abandoned after three of the interrogators died during implementation.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.700
Autopsies revealed that their central nervous systems were completely fried.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:10.940
They're not like me.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.940
I can do this.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:26.990
Clark, your body may be...

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:30.990
Your body may be invincible, but who's to say your mind isn't vulnerable somehow?

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.990
It's my fault that care is missing.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.990
Using technology built by Lionel Luther?

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:36.990
God only knows why he created that thing.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.990
Lana, there's no other choice.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.990
Clark, just be careful, okay?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:45.990
I watched three field officers die after their brains went into electro-neuro shock.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.990
This machine is a death trap.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:51.990
I pay you a small fortune, doctor, so please withhold your negative opinions.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:58.100
Ladies, would you please wait outside?

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:10.779
Lex wakes up.

00:10:10.779 --> 00:10:11.779
wakes up.

00:10:11.779 --> 00:10:13.779
You'll never know I was in there, right?

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:17.779
In a few successful cases, the terrorists had no memory of the process.

00:10:17.779 --> 00:10:21.779
Now, the freshest memories will most likely be the first ones in.

00:10:21.779 --> 00:10:23.779
The deeper you get, the greater the risk.

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:27.779
If your brainwave show any sign of duress, I will pull you from the procedure.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:29.779
I don't plan on staying in there very long.

00:10:29.779 --> 00:10:33.779
The software has been encoded with what you will see as a red door.

00:10:33.779 --> 00:10:35.779
That is your emergency exit.

00:10:35.779 --> 00:10:39.779
That red door, Clark, you must never lose track of that.

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:45.779
If we get disconnected, it's the only link between Lex's subconscious and reality.

00:10:45.779 --> 00:10:52.740
Let's get this over with.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:53.740
Right.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.740
I just relax and stay still.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:56.740
Procedure is painless.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:13:12.710
Entering further into this.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:14:06.039
Second vest.

00:14:06.039 --> 00:14:08.039
I'll pass that along to the kitchen.

00:14:08.039 --> 00:14:11.440
Give them some incentive.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:16.889
Lex.

00:14:16.889 --> 00:14:17.889
Linda.

00:14:17.889 --> 00:14:21.649
Doesn't suit you.

00:14:21.649 --> 00:14:24.649
Really? Who do I, uh, look like?

00:14:24.649 --> 00:14:25.649
I don't know.

00:14:25.649 --> 00:14:27.649
Someone who doesn't belong here, that's for sure.

00:14:27.649 --> 00:14:31.700
I think that I go again with my opinions.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:38.779
What do I know?

00:14:38.779 --> 00:14:41.779
You know, some days, I don't even know what I'm doing here.

00:14:41.779 --> 00:14:47.590
That apron's not chained to the counter.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:51.980
I lost to go.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:58.190
It's sort of embarrassing, but, um, but a month ago, I lost me.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:13.919
I'm not sure you'd be interested.

00:15:13.919 --> 00:15:14.919
I know some of the past researchers.

00:15:14.919 --> 00:15:25.139
Maybe one can help you.

00:15:25.139 --> 00:15:26.139
What are you doing?

00:15:26.139 --> 00:15:53.159
I don't remember.

00:15:53.159 --> 00:15:54.159
Who are you?

00:15:54.159 --> 00:15:57.600
I'm Alexander.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:07.059
Why we want to kill you, you're the good part of him, aren't you?

00:16:07.059 --> 00:16:08.059
He said they're making me.

00:16:08.059 --> 00:16:11.059
And if he wants us, go kill us.

00:16:11.059 --> 00:16:21.259
I'm looking for two women.

00:16:21.259 --> 00:16:24.590
You know what they are?

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:32.950
Let's never visit.

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.950
You'll be safe in there.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:35.950
Trust me.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.950
You're my best friend.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:53.720
The brainwave activity.

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:57.509
It's too high.

00:16:57.509 --> 00:16:59.509
He appears to be going in deep.

00:16:59.509 --> 00:17:02.509
If Clark's gone in too far, he might never find his way out.

00:17:02.509 --> 00:17:04.509
The pressure's dropping.

00:17:04.509 --> 00:17:06.509
I've never seen this before, sir.

00:17:06.509 --> 00:17:07.509
I don't know what's going on.

00:17:07.509 --> 00:17:41.490
What is the rule about my briefcase?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.490
Alexander?

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.490
Don't ever, ever, ever touch.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:44.690
Don't ever touch it.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.190
Yeah.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:50.200
And you know I can tell when it's been opened.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:53.589
Did you open it?

00:17:53.589 --> 00:17:56.650
Did you?

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:57.750
No.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:58.750
I swear.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.549
Dad, I didn't touch it.

00:18:00.549 --> 00:18:01.349
Don't.

00:18:01.349 --> 00:18:06.250
Lie to me, Lex.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.349
Don't make excuses.

00:18:07.349 --> 00:18:10.920
All right.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.720
Be a man, Lex.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.720
And admit what you've done.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.920
Admit it!

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.119
But I didn't do it!

00:18:17.119 --> 00:18:18.720
I don't care about your wife!

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:21.259
All right, Lex.

00:18:21.259 --> 00:18:23.160
If it wasn't you, then it was it.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:23.660
Hmm?

00:18:23.759 --> 00:18:25.759
Answer me.

00:18:25.759 --> 00:18:27.759
Who opened my briefcase?

00:18:27.759 --> 00:18:29.759
Answer me, Lex!

00:18:29.759 --> 00:18:31.759
Mom!

00:18:37.809 --> 00:18:40.809
I saw her in your office going through your stuff.

00:18:40.809 --> 00:18:43.809
She told me not to say anything.

00:18:43.809 --> 00:18:45.809
You let go of him.

00:18:45.809 --> 00:18:49.630
I had to know the truth.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.630
Veritas.

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.630
What is it?

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:59.349
I'm tired of the secrets.

00:18:59.349 --> 00:19:02.349
You'll listen back at your meetings.

00:19:02.349 --> 00:19:03.349
Please!

00:19:03.349 --> 00:19:04.349
What are you keeping from me?

00:19:04.349 --> 00:19:07.349
What are you doing for these people?

00:19:07.349 --> 00:19:15.859
You keep out of my business, Lillian.

00:19:15.859 --> 00:19:26.230
Sorry.

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:31.079
You've said enough.

00:19:31.079 --> 00:20:21.049
Patron's sin of lost souls.

00:20:21.049 --> 00:20:25.869
You know, Finley said all you really care about is money.

00:20:25.869 --> 00:20:28.869
But it's people, isn't it, Lex?

00:20:28.869 --> 00:20:35.900
I did my research.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.900
You're a humanitarian.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.900
All the hospitals you built, the scholarships you funded.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:43.900
And along the way, I've seen a lot of people get the help they need.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.900
Look, everything's been arranged.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:46.900
My jet sons are.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.880
stand by to take you to treatment.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:52.880
So this is really happening, then.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:55.880
I guess we'll find out if you're flying.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.880
Whatever you find out, I'll be by your side every step of the way.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:02.670
I just don't want this to work.

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.670
Trust me.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:07.670
There's nothing that's laws that can't be found again.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:16.599
I'm going to go thank Finley and say goodbye to everyone.

00:21:16.599 --> 00:21:33.450
Quite the charmer, aren't you?

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:38.269
You're a little out of your way for a club sandwich, Lois.

00:21:38.269 --> 00:21:40.269
What the hell are you doing here?

00:21:40.269 --> 00:21:41.269
Well, I figured you weren't in Detroit.

00:21:41.269 --> 00:21:43.269
I figured you weren't in Detroit for the electric car show,

00:21:43.269 --> 00:21:45.769
but I never would have guessed a secret rendezvous

00:21:45.769 --> 00:21:46.769
with Clark's cousin.

00:21:46.769 --> 00:21:48.269
I'm helping her.

00:21:48.269 --> 00:21:49.769
Never heard that one before.

00:21:49.769 --> 00:21:53.769
Look, I don't expect you to understand.

00:21:53.769 --> 00:21:55.769
You're right.

00:21:55.769 --> 00:21:57.769
I work better with visual aids.

00:21:57.769 --> 00:22:00.269
And now that I think about it, Clark does too.

00:22:00.269 --> 00:22:06.059
What the hell are you doing?

00:22:06.059 --> 00:22:07.059
No!

00:22:07.059 --> 00:22:16.559
What is it? What's happening?

00:22:16.559 --> 00:22:18.559
The EEG, it's showing Delta Wave entrainment.

00:22:18.559 --> 00:22:19.559
They're in phase.

00:22:19.559 --> 00:22:20.559
You're nervous.

00:22:20.559 --> 00:22:21.559
Why?

00:22:21.559 --> 00:22:23.059
The subject is in too deep.

00:22:23.059 --> 00:22:25.559
We've never been able to get anyone back from this point.

00:22:25.559 --> 00:22:28.980
All right, all right.

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:30.980
Terminate the procedure.

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:31.980
Pull Clark out.

00:22:31.980 --> 00:22:33.980
Now, I already tried.

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:34.980
He's trapped, Mr. Luther.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:38.980
As long as their brainwaves are synchronized, I can't separate them.

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:40.980
Now it's up to Clark to exit on his own.

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:52.390
I always knew there was a voyeur lurking behind that telescope.

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:54.390
Look, I don't want any trouble.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.390
Forgive me.

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:58.390
I've been a terrible host.

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:17.579
Let me give you the Grand Tour.

00:23:17.579 --> 00:23:18.579
Just getting good.

00:23:18.579 --> 00:25:33.640
If we lose him, we lose them both.

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:40.000
We have four minutes to bring them back before brain death.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:43.299
Charge!

00:25:43.299 --> 00:25:58.289
He came so long.

00:25:58.289 --> 00:26:00.289
Oh, my God.

00:26:00.289 --> 00:26:01.289
Charge!

00:26:01.289 --> 00:26:02.289
Clear!

00:26:02.289 --> 00:26:03.289
You shouldn't be in here, Miss Sullivan.

00:26:03.289 --> 00:26:04.289
What's happening?

00:26:04.289 --> 00:26:05.289
Why are they not waking Clark up?

00:26:05.289 --> 00:26:06.289
He's in Lex's mind.

00:26:06.289 --> 00:26:07.289
He's trapped.

00:26:07.289 --> 00:26:10.289
If Lex dies, then Clark dies with him.

00:26:10.289 --> 00:26:15.150
Sir, they've lost him.

00:26:15.150 --> 00:26:22.400
I can save them.

00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:26.349
How?

00:26:26.349 --> 00:26:28.349
Just trust me, Mr. Luther, I can.

00:26:28.349 --> 00:26:59.539
You're holding me back, Alexander.

00:26:59.539 --> 00:27:00.539
Stop!

00:27:00.539 --> 00:27:08.009
It's time to say goodbye.

00:27:08.009 --> 00:29:55.410
No!

00:29:55.410 --> 00:29:58.140
Just get her to her apartment.

00:29:58.140 --> 00:30:01.140
Clark, she's barely alive.

00:30:01.140 --> 00:30:03.140
Trust me, doctors can do nothing for her.

00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:12.819
Are you sure you know what you're doing?

00:30:12.819 --> 00:30:15.819
When your dad locks your car in storage,

00:30:15.819 --> 00:30:17.819
because you snuck up to see your boyfriend's band,

00:30:17.819 --> 00:30:19.819
you learn a few tricks.

00:30:19.819 --> 00:30:24.309
Bingo.

00:30:24.309 --> 00:30:40.440
We're gonna have to have to have to do you.

00:30:40.440 --> 00:31:01.309
find another way out. After everything that I've done for you?

00:31:01.309 --> 00:31:06.309
Look, before you get all trigger happy again, let's be rational.

00:31:06.309 --> 00:31:11.319
I am rational, but I just killed a man.

00:31:11.319 --> 00:31:16.339
This isn't how it was supposed to happen.

00:31:16.339 --> 00:31:20.339
Linda, I just wanted to protect you.

00:31:20.339 --> 00:31:22.339
I know what it's like to start over.

00:31:22.339 --> 00:31:29.640
People take advantage of you. They look at you different.

00:31:29.640 --> 00:31:36.349
I am different. And I'm not Linda.

00:31:36.349 --> 00:31:39.680
What are you doing?

00:31:39.680 --> 00:31:40.680
What are you doing?

00:31:40.680 --> 00:31:47.190
If you want to kill Lois, you'll have to kill me.

00:31:47.190 --> 00:31:54.519
If you don't come with me, you're just going to turn me in.

00:31:54.519 --> 00:32:57.759
And I can't go back to prison.

00:32:57.759 --> 00:33:02.359
You had this worried today.

00:33:02.359 --> 00:33:05.849
How are you feeling?

00:33:05.849 --> 00:33:09.390
That's the problem, Dad.

00:33:09.390 --> 00:33:10.390
I feel fine.

00:33:10.390 --> 00:33:13.700
What's going on?

00:33:13.700 --> 00:33:16.700
I'm admitted here with a bullet in my head,

00:33:16.700 --> 00:33:18.700
and now there's not so much as a scratch on me.

00:33:18.700 --> 00:33:20.700
You can thank your friend.

00:33:20.700 --> 00:33:22.700
Oliver Queen, the healing technology.

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:25.700
The healing technology developed by Queen Laboratories,

00:33:25.700 --> 00:33:28.700
you of all people should remember that.

00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:31.700
I was any of the impression that all the serum was destroyed.

00:33:31.700 --> 00:33:35.700
Now, all but a single dose, which I salvaged,

00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:41.809
for myself, if I should ever need it.

00:33:41.809 --> 00:33:44.809
But you gave it to me.

00:33:44.809 --> 00:33:46.809
You sound surprised.

00:33:46.809 --> 00:33:49.809
You're my son. You think I'd stand there and watch you die?

00:33:49.809 --> 00:34:08.820
Honestly, Dad, I don't know.

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:09.820
Today, I...

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:23.880
I realized when there is something I was afraid

00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:25.880
that I would never have the chance to tell you.

00:34:25.880 --> 00:34:30.989
Yeah? And what's that?

00:34:30.989 --> 00:35:23.719
See me, you know, dead, did she?

00:35:23.719 --> 00:35:25.719
No, she had a street back to the planet

00:35:25.719 --> 00:35:29.840
to write a story about what happened in Detroit.

00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:31.840
Likes will kill that story in a heartbeat.

00:35:31.840 --> 00:35:35.309
Speaking of heartbeats,

00:35:35.309 --> 00:35:37.309
you didn't have one for over 18 hours.

00:35:37.309 --> 00:35:46.480
Look, I was hoping we could skip the lecture

00:35:46.480 --> 00:35:48.480
and go straight to the welcome back dinner. I'm starving.

00:35:48.480 --> 00:35:50.480
It's 15 hours longer than the last time, Chloe.

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:53.760
I've been sitting here literally

00:35:53.760 --> 00:35:55.760
trying to think about what to say at your funeral.

00:35:55.760 --> 00:35:59.840
Well, let's both be glad that I'm alive,

00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:02.840
because I know how much you hate giving speeches.

00:36:02.840 --> 00:36:06.119
Chloe, I appreciate what you did for me.

00:36:06.119 --> 00:36:08.119
It goes beyond friendship.

00:36:08.119 --> 00:36:10.119
But you can never do it again.

00:36:10.119 --> 00:36:12.119
Look, I have the power to save people's lives.

00:36:12.119 --> 00:36:16.119
Now, obviously, I am the last person who thought she would drag Lex back

00:36:16.119 --> 00:36:19.119
from the clutches of death, but it was my decision to make.

00:36:19.119 --> 00:36:31.519
Of course it was.

00:36:31.519 --> 00:36:32.519
But you know, you're not wrong.

00:36:32.519 --> 00:36:33.519
I mean, is.

00:36:33.519 --> 00:36:39.789
As great as this power is, it does come with a lot of consequences.

00:36:39.789 --> 00:36:42.789
And I think that one of the responsibilities for both of us

00:36:42.789 --> 00:36:45.789
is staying alive.

00:36:45.789 --> 00:36:53.760
Maybe I am pushing my luck with this whole death thing.

00:36:53.760 --> 00:36:55.760
I mean, it is death, after all.

00:36:55.760 --> 00:37:10.789
Does that mean you're never going to use your abilities again?

00:37:10.789 --> 00:37:13.789
It means I'm more confused now than ever.

00:37:13.789 --> 00:37:18.610
Out of the entire catalog of meteor abilities,

00:37:18.610 --> 00:37:22.610
why was I the one chosen to be in charge of such an amazing gift?

00:37:22.610 --> 00:37:45.880
It's like a refueling.

00:37:45.880 --> 00:37:48.880
I see you and start defending myself.

00:37:48.880 --> 00:37:50.880
Well, that's what guilt does to a person.

00:37:50.880 --> 00:37:54.199
What were you doing in Detroit with Kara?

00:37:54.199 --> 00:37:56.199
I was trying to help her.

00:37:56.199 --> 00:38:01.980
And she ended up kidnapped.

00:38:01.980 --> 00:38:03.980
You knew she had amnesia.

00:38:03.980 --> 00:38:05.980
Sure, what she told me?

00:38:05.980 --> 00:38:07.980
That's when I volunteered my help.

00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:12.519
Did it ever occur to you to pick up a phone and call me?

00:38:12.519 --> 00:38:14.519
I did call, twice.

00:38:14.519 --> 00:38:17.519
Lana hung up on me before I could get a word out.

00:38:17.519 --> 00:38:26.019
Do you even know when you're lying anymore?

00:38:26.019 --> 00:38:32.019
You know, I've stopped pretending to care whether or not you believe me, so why don't you?

00:38:32.019 --> 00:38:37.190
Because I do care, Lex.

00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:44.190
And there's a side of you that knows what's right.

00:38:44.190 --> 00:38:45.190
Wow.

00:38:45.190 --> 00:38:49.190
Now what would I do without Clark Kent, voice of reason?

00:38:49.190 --> 00:38:51.190
That voice isn't me, Lex. It's you.

00:38:51.190 --> 00:38:56.500
They're still good inside of you. Let that voice lead you back to it.

00:38:56.500 --> 00:39:00.500
I did know it would only take a brush with death to see your softer side.

00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:07.050
Trust me, Lex, there's nothing that's lost that can't be found again.

00:39:07.050 --> 00:39:33.940
Anything.

00:39:33.940 --> 00:39:37.309
Good?

00:39:37.309 --> 00:39:38.309
Um, I don't know.

00:39:38.309 --> 00:39:40.309
Supposed that this is one of my favorite songs,

00:39:40.309 --> 00:39:42.309
and I don't even remember how it goes.

00:39:42.309 --> 00:39:46.840
Lex, I saw what happened.

00:39:46.840 --> 00:39:51.929
They were bleeding.

00:39:51.929 --> 00:39:54.929
I told you, I know some talented doctors.

00:39:54.929 --> 00:40:05.480
Obviously, you too.

00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:07.480
So, uh, I guess I used to work here.

00:40:07.480 --> 00:40:10.480
I wonder it'll give you my job back.

00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:18.630
Well, I think the owner will understand.

00:40:18.630 --> 00:40:20.630
Thank you for meeting me.

00:40:20.630 --> 00:40:22.630
I mean, home isn't feeling very...

00:40:22.630 --> 00:40:23.630
Tamaya?

00:40:23.630 --> 00:40:29.019
I mean, Clark seems like a really nice guy and everything,

00:40:29.019 --> 00:40:30.019
but...

00:40:30.019 --> 00:40:33.019
I can't help it feeling he's hiding something from me.

00:40:33.019 --> 00:40:38.940
As his former best friend, I know the feeling all too well.

00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:41.940
See, Clark didn't even mention that you guys were friends.

00:40:41.940 --> 00:40:50.440
What happened?

00:40:50.440 --> 00:40:58.590
I grew up. I'm not interested in keeping secrets.

00:40:58.590 --> 00:41:03.670
This treatment will help you get your memories back, and with it,

00:41:03.670 --> 00:41:05.670
we'll get the truth.

00:41:05.670 --> 00:41:11.570
Once and for all.

